            </div>
        
            <div id="metadata" style="display: none;"><div data-category="settings" data-key="shell style" data-value-type="json">"boxed"</div><div data-category="main" data-key="header" data-value-type="html"></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Arithmetic in <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{Q}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span></h1>
<p>The Arithmetic Rule for the rationals is a special built-in validation tool that Lurch provides for evaluating arithmetic identities and inequalities involving rational numbers.</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Arithmetic in the Rationals Rule. </strong>We allow <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Arithmetic(QQ)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Arithmetic</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.16667em; height: 0.85556em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> to justify equations or inequality which only involves natural number constants (e.g. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;-2&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−2</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;3/5, &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">3/5,</span></span></span></span></span>...), the operators <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\cdot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;/&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">/</span></span></span></span></span>and&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\^&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">^</span></span></span></span></span> and the relations <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;=&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;&lt;&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<p>If a the meaningful expression 'by arithmetic' follows a claim, Lurch will try to use the CAS&nbsp;<a href="http://algebrite.org">Algebrite </a>to determine if the given claim is valid.&nbsp; The claim must be an equation or inequality which only involves natural number constants (e.g. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;2&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;3, &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">3,</span></span></span></span></span>...), the operators <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\cdot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\^&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">^</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;/&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">/</span></span></span></span></span>, and the relations <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;=&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;&lt;&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span></span></span></span></span>. For example, it can check something like this:</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\frac{12}{14}=\\frac{7-1}{7}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">14</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">12</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">7</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">7</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> by arithmetic</p>
<p>and inequalities like this</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\frac{6}{13}&lt;\\frac{4}{7}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">13</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">6</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">7</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">4</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> by arithmetic</p>
<p>but will be inapplicable to something like this because it has a non-integer exponent</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;2^\\frac{1}{2}&lt;2&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.16em;"><span style="top: -3.48em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 1.05em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.97em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.46em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 71.43%;"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 71.43%;"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__cmr">2</span></span></span></span></span> by arithmetic</p>
<p>or something like this because it divides by zero</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\frac{0}{2^{10}-1024}=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 1.15em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.83em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.75em;"><span style="top: -3.28em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.46em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">10</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__cmr">1024</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.65em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span> by arithmetic</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">It is also inapplicable for something like this, because it contains a variable</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;0\\leq x^2&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.46em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> by arithmetic</p>
<hr>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Arithmetic-rationals-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><div>
<h1>Number Systems</h1>
</div>
<p>We can define the natural, integers and rational numbers as subsets of the real numbers.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare natural, integer, rational, irrational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare natural number, integer, rational, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__text">irrational</span></span></span></span></span> to be constants.&nbsp; Note that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{N}, \\mathbb{Z}, \\mathbb{Q}, \\mathbb{R}, \\mathbb{C}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__bb">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__bb">C</span></span></span></span></span> are declared to be constants by default.</p>
<p><span style="font-size: 17.16px;"><strong>Terminology</strong></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Natural.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is a natural number equiv  x in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is a natural number</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Integer.</strong> &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is an integer equiv x in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is an integer</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Rational.&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is rational equiv x in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is rational</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Irrational.</strong>&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is irrational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is irrational</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;equiv&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;≡&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in RR, &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is not rational&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is not rational</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<h3>Relationships between the sets</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Natural Numbers</strong></p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0 in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-1 notin NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span><span class="ML__cmr">∉</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>3. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n+1 in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span><br>4. If <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathcal{P}(0)\\text{ and }\\forall k\\in\\mathbb{N}.\\mathcal{P}(k)\\Rightarrow\\mathcal{P}(k+1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__cmr">(0)</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1)</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\forall n \\in \\mathbb{N}.\\mathcal{P}(n)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; (see the rules for induction below)</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Integers&nbsp; </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n in ZZ equiv n in NN or -n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Rational Numbers&nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if x = a/b, b neq 0, a in ZZ, b in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Rational Numbers&nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If r in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;r=a/b for some a,b in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Positives &nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in A^+ &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot; equiv&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;≡&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in A, 0&lt;x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Integers. </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If -n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot; n in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Non-negative Integers.</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n in NN equiv n in ZZ, 0 leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Inclusions.</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;NN subset ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊆</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;NN subset QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊆</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;NN in RR&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">R</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;ZZ subset QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊆</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;ZZ subset RR&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊆</span><span class="ML__bb">R</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;QQ in RR&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Q</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Closure of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{N}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>. </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN, m in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n+m in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n*m in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>, and&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n^m in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.72em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Closure of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{Z}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>. </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in ZZ, m in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n+m in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n*m in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n-m in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if k in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n^k in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.9em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Closure of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{Q}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>. </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in QQ, m in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n+m in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n*m in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n-m in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n/m in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span> (if <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;m\\neq 0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span>) and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if k in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n^k in QQ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.9em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Q</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Partial Closure of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\N&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>.</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If m,n in NN, m leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text">and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n-m in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">m</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div>
<div>
<h3>Induction</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Induction</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(0)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let k in NN be such that @P(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text"> be such that </span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(k+1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall n in NN.@P(n)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Strong induction</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(0)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let k in NN be such that (forall j in NN.j leq k implies @P(j))&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text"> be such that </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">j</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">j</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.85396em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">j</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(k+1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall n in NN.@P(n)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Induction from <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span></strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let k in NN be such that a leq k and @P(k)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text"> be such that </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__text"> and </span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(k+1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
