        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Sequences-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;dependency&quot;" data-metadata_description="&quot;none&quot;" data-metadata_filename="&quot;learn/algebra/rules/Algebra-Rules.lurch&quot;" data-metadata_source="&quot;the web&quot;" data-metadata_auto-refresh="true" style="border: 1px solid gray; padding: 0px 1em;"><div class="lurch-atom-metadata" style="display: none;"><div data-key="content">
            <div id="loadlink">
                <p><a>Open this file in the Lurch web app</a></p>
                
            </div>
        
            <div id="metadata" style="display: none;"><div data-category="settings" data-key="shell style" data-value-type="json">"boxed"</div><div data-category="main" data-key="header" data-value-type="html"></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Algebra</h1>
<p>The Algebra Rule is a special built-in validation tool that Lurch provides for evaluating algebraic identities. It does not import any additional libraries.</p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Algebra.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;The <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;AlgebraRule&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">algebra rule</span></span></span></span></span> uses a computer algebra system to evaluate algebraic identities (equations only) and also inequalities that are supported by the Arithmetic Rule for rational numbers.</p>
</div>
<p>If a the meaningful expression 'by algebra' follows a claim, Lurch will try to use the computer algebra system <a href="http://algebrite.org">Algebrite </a>to determine if the given claim is valid.&nbsp; The claim must be an equation. For example, it can check something like this:</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x^2-1=(x-1)\\cdot(x+1)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.46em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__cmr">1)</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1)</span></span></span></span></span> by algebra</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">It also will use the computer algebra system to check inequalities that are supported by the built-in validation tool for arithmetic over the rational numbers, namely ones that only involve the natural number constants <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;0,1,2,3,\\ldots&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">2,</span><span class="ML__cmr">3,</span><span class="ML__cmr">…</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;the operators <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\cdot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\text{^}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">^</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;/&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">/</span></span></span></span></span>, and the relations <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;=&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">=</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\neq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\leq&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span></span></span></span></span>, and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\lt&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span></span></span></span></span>. Exponents must be&nbsp;integers and you cannot divide by zero.&nbsp;</p>
<p>But will be inapplicable to something like this because it is not an equation and contains a variable.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;0&lt;x^2&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.46em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> by algebra</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Whether allowing such a rule will allow someone to prove a contradiction by exploiting something like e.g.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\frac{x}{x}=1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mfrac"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.31em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3.5em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span> by algebra</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">in a proof where <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;x=0&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span></span></span></span></span> is a possibility to consider when using this rule in any document or library, i.e., use at your own risk.</p>
<hr>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Algebra-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Common Notions</h1>
<p>We provide some definitions and elementary theorems that are usually assumed as background in a typical undergraduate math course.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare finite&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare finite</span></span></span></span></span> to be a constant.</p>
<h3>Definitions (typed quantifiers)</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\forall+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span> (typed)</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let s in S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(s)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall x in S.@P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\forall+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span> (typed)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If forall x in S.@P(x), t in S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(t)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.61508em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\exists+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span> (typed)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If t in S, @P(t)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.61508em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;exists x in S.@P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\exists-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span> <strong>(typed) </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If exists x in S.@P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;@P(s) for some s in S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\exists!+&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃!</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span></span></span></span></span> (<strong>typed)&nbsp;</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;t in S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span><br><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(t)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.61508em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let y in S be such that 𝜆P(y)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> be such that </span></span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.625em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;y=t&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;exists!x in S.𝜆P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃!</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\exists!-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃!</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span> (<strong>typed)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;exists!x in S.𝜆P(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∃!</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;𝜆P(c), &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall y.𝜆P(y) implies y=c for some c in S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">P</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.625em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<h3><strong>Theorems</strong></h3>
<h4><strong>Set Theory</strong></h4>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (trivial subsets)</strong></p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.087%; border-width: 0px;" border="1"><colgroup><col style="width: 33.2168%;"><col style="width: 33.2168%;"><col style="width: 33.2168%;"></colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="border-width: 0px;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;{} subset A&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊆</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span></span></span></span></span></td>
