<p><strong>Equivalence Relations</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (equivalence class partition) </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If rel is a relation on A, a,b in A, rel is an equivalence relation &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__ams">∽</span><span class="ML__text"> is a relation on </span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__ams">∽</span><span class="ML__text"> is an equivalence relation</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a rel b equiv class(a)=class(b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__ams">∽</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span> and</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;neg (a rel b) equiv class(a) cap class(b) = {}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">¬</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__ams">∽</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∩</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
