<p><strong>Basic Combinatorics</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (finite)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;S is finite equiv card(S) in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__text"> is finite</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (same cardinality) &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If f:S to T, f is bijective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">T</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;card(S)=card(T)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">T</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (same cardinality) &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If card(S)=card(T)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">T</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f:S to T, f is bijective for some f&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">T</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective for some </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{O}_n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">O</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in OO_(n) equiv x in NN, x leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">O</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathbb{I}_n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">I</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in II_(n) equiv x in NN,1 leq x leq n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">I</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">≤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;card(OO_(n))=n+1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.16667em; height: 0.85556em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__bb">O</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">+</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;card(II_(n))=n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.83889em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__bb">I</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<hr>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</div></div>
