            <div id="document"><h1>Primality in <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\Z&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span></h1>
<p>&nbsp;See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare composite, prime, nu&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare composite, prime</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="lcGreek ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.07em;">ν</span></span></span></span></span> to be a constant.</p>
<h3>Definitions</h3>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Composite</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in ZZ, n is composite&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> is composite</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;k|abs(n),1&lt;k&lt;abs(n) for some k in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Composite</strong> &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in ZZ, k in NN, 1&lt;k&lt;abs(n), k|n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">k</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n is composite&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> is composite</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Prime</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;n is prime equiv 1&lt;abs(n), n is not composite&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text"> is not composite</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span>-adic order &nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n,p in ZZ setminus {0}, p is prime&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span></span></span></span></span> then the&nbsp;<em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span>-adic order</em> of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>, denoted <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\nu_p(n)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="lcGreek ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.07em;">ν</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp;is the highest power of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span> that divides <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>, i.e., <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;nu_(p)(n) in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="lcGreek ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.07em;">ν</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> and</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p^(nu_(p)(n)) | n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="lcGreek ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.07em;">ν</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.17em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.45em; display: inline-block; font-size: 71.43%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p^(nu_(p)(n)+1) ndiv n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.94em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.73em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="lcGreek ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.07em;">ν</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.17em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.45em; display: inline-block; font-size: 71.43%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">+1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__ams">∤</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p><strong>Theorems</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (divisors of primes)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If p in ZZ, p is prime&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p notin {-1,0,1}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∉</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8388800000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If c|p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;c in {-p,-1,1,p}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8388800000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1,</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (divisors of primes)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p in ZZ setminus {-1,0,1}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8388800000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let c in ZZ, c|p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;c in {-p,-1,1,p}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8388800000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1,</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p is prime&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (relatively prime divisor)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If a, b, c in ZZ, a neq 0 or b neq 0, a|b*c, gcd(a,b)=1&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__text">gcd</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a | c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (mutual divisors)&nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If a,b in ZZ, a|b, b|a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a=b or a=-b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (alternate definition of prime)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If p,b,c in ZZ, p is prime, p|b*c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p|b or p|c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (alternate definition of prime)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If p in ZZ setminus {-1,0,1}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8388800000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span> and</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let b,c in ZZ, p|b*c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋅</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p|b or p|c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p is prime&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic - existence)&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in ZZ setminus {-1,0,1}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8388800000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p|n, p is prime for some p in ZZ&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; Thus, every integer in <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\Z\\setminus\\{-1,0,1\\}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__cmr">{−1,</span><span class="ML__cmr">0,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1}</span></span></span></span></span> is a product of primes.</p>
</div>
<p><strong>Theorem (Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic - uniqueness)&nbsp;</strong>The power of every prime divisor <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> is <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\nu_p(n)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="lcGreek ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.07em;">ν</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span></span></span></span></span>, so the prime factorization of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span> is unique.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</div></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Ch-1-3-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Algebra in <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\Z_{n}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p>There are no new constants.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem.</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If p in ZZ,1&lt;p&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__cmr">&lt;</span><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span></span> then the following are equivalent.</p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;p is prime  equiv&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span><span class="ML__text"> is prime</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall A in ZZ_(p) setminus class(0).exists X in ZZ_(p).A otimes X=class(1) equiv &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊗</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>3. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;forall A in ZZ_(p).forall B in ZZ_(p).A odot B = class(0) implies A=class(0) or B=class(0)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.44em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">p</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⇒</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.64444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<hr>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
