            <div id="document"><h1>Definition and Examples of Rings</h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare ring, commutative, unit, intdomain, field, subring, has, identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare ring, commutative, unit, integral domain, field, </span><span class="ML__cmr">⊑</span><span class="ML__text">, has</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__text">identity</span></span></span></span></span> to be constants.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Ring 0. </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;oplus:R cross R to R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;odot:R cross R to R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0_(R) in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Ring I.&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, x in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;<br>(identity of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0_(R) oplus x = x = x oplus 0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>(inverse of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-x in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus (-x) = 0_(R) = (-x) oplus x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Ring II.&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, x, y in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p>(closure) <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus y in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot y in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span><br>(commutativity of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus y = y oplus x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Ring III.&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, x, y, z in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then<br>(associativity of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus (y oplus z) = (x oplus y) oplus z &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
(associativity of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\odot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot (y odot z) = (x odot y) odot z &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>
<p>(distributivity of&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\odot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span></span></span></span></span> over <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot (y oplus z) = (x odot y) oplus (x odot z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(y oplus z) odot x = (y odot x) oplus (z odot x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>&nbsp;Definition of Ring.</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p>1. (closure)<em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;oplus:R cross R to R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>,</em><em>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;odot:R cross R to R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;O in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let x,y, z in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. (associativity of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus (y oplus z) = (x oplus y) oplus z &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>3. (commutativity of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus y = y oplus x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>4. (identity of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>)&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;O oplus x = x = x oplus O&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>5. (inverse of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x oplus X = O = X oplus x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>6. (associativity of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\odot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot (y odot z) = (x odot y) odot z &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>7. (distributivity of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\odot&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span></span></span></span></span> over <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\oplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot (y oplus z) = (x odot y) oplus (x odot z)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(y oplus z) odot x = (y odot x) oplus (z odot x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7777700000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;Then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R,oplus,odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (uniqueness of additive identity).</strong></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring, O in R, forall x in R. O oplus x = x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;O=0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">O</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (commutative ring)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring, R is commutative, x,y in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot y = y odot x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (commutative ring)</strong> &nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R,oplus, odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let x,y in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x odot y=y odot x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;R is commutative&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (ring with identity)</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring, R has identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1_(R) in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if x in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1_(R) odot x = x = x odot 1_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (ring with identity)</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R, oplus, odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;I in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let x in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;I odot x = x = x odot I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude&nbsp; </em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot; R has identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;I = 1_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (multiplicative inverse)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R has identity, x in R, x is a unit of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity, </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is a unit of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x^- in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x^- odot x = 1_(R) = x odot x^-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (unit) and Theorem (uniqueness)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring, R has identity, x,X in R, x odot X = 1_(R) = X odot x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity, </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x is a unit in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is a unit in </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;X=x^-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (integral domain)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring, R is an integral domain&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is an integral domain</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;R is commutative&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;R has identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span></span></span></span></span><br>3. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;1_(R) neq 0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>4. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If a,b in R, a odot b = 0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a=0_(R) or b=0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (integral domain)</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
