            <div id="document"><h1>Algebra in Rings</h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare Units, assoc&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare </span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋄</span></span></span></span></span> to be constants.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (the sign theorem 0) </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;0_(R) in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-0_(R)=0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (the sign theorem 1)</strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a odot 0_(R)=0_(R)=0_(R) odot a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>3. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-(-a)=a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>7. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If R has identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-1_(R) odot a=-a=a odot (-1_(R))&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.79444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (the sign theorem 2)</strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, a,b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a odot (-b)=-(a odot b)=(-a) odot b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
<p>4.&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-(a oplus b)=-a oplus (-b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>5. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;-(a oplus (-b))=-a oplus b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>6. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(-a) odot (-b)=a odot b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Corollary (to sign thm 1.1)&nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, a,b,c in R, a neq 0_(R), a=b odot c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;b neq 0_(R) or c neq 0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> or </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\mathcal{U}(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__cmr">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">)</span></span></span></span></span>) </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R has identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Units(R) subset R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in Units(R) equiv x is a unit of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text"> is a unit of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (associate) &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R is commutative, R has identity, a,b,u in R, u in Units(R), a=u odot b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a is an associate of b &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text"> is an associate of </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span>. This can also be&nbsp; written <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;a \\diamond b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋄</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span> (and entered as <code>a assoc b</code>).</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (associate) &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R is commutative, R has identity, a,b in R,&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a is an associate of b &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text"> is an associate of </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a=u odot b for some u in Units(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (units are invertible)</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;<em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R has identity, a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></em> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a^- in Units(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;(a^-)^-=a&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.821331em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size1">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size1">)</span></span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.99em;"><span style="top: -3.57em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (cancellation in integral domains)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Suppose [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R is an integral domain, a,b,c in R, a neq 0_(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Suppose </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is an integral domain, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__rlap"><span class="ML__inner"><span class="ML__cmr"></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; Then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if a odot b=a odot c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;b=c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (fields are integral domains)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, R is a field&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is a field</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;R is an integral domain&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is an integral domain</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Ch-3-2-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Ring Homomorphisms</h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare homomorphism, isomorphism, isom&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare homomorphism, isomorphism</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">≅</span></span></span></span></span> to be constants.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (homomorphism)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is a homomorphism, a,b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p>1.<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(a oplus b)=f(a) boxplus f(b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(a odot b)=f(a) boxdot f(b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (homomorphism)</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R,oplus,odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f:R to S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let a,b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(a oplus b)=f(a) boxplus f(b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(a odot b)=f(a) boxdot f(b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (composition of injections)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If f:A to B, g:B to C, f is injective, g is injective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">C</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is injective</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__text"> is injective</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;g comp f is injective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">∘</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is injective</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p>&nbsp;<strong>Theorem (composition of surjections) </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If f:A to B, g:B to C, f is surjective, g is surjective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">C</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is surjective</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__text"> is surjective</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;g comp f is surjective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">∘</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is surjective</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (composition of bijections)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If f:A to B, g:B to C, f is bijective, g is bijective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">B</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">C</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;g comp f is bijective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">∘</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p style="text-align: left;"><strong>Definition (isomorphism)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is an isomorphism equiv f is a homomorphism, f is bijective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is an isomorphism</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p style="text-align: left;"><strong>Definition (isomorphic)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is an isomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is an isomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;R is isomorphic to S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is isomorphic to </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span>. We will also write <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;R \\cong S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">≅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span> for this (entered as&nbsp;<code>R isom S</code>).</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (composition of homomorphisms)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[T,dotplus, oast] is a ring, f:R to S, f is a homomorphism,&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8866799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">T</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">∔</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊛</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;g:S to T, g is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">T</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;g comp f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">g</span><span class="ML__cmr">∘</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (inverse isomorphism) </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is an isomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is an isomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f^(-1) is an isomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.87em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.51em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> is an isomorphism</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (properties of homomorphisms I)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(0_(R))=0_(S)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.79444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(-a)=-f(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>3. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(a oplus (-b))=f(a) boxplus (-f(b))&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (properties of homomorphisms II)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f:R to S, f is a homomorphism, R has identity, &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is surjective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is surjective</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p>4. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;S has identity&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>5. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(1_(R))=1_(S)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.79444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>6 .<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if u in Units(R)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(u) in Units(S)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(u^-)=(f(u))^-&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.821331em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size1">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size1">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (homomorphic image)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f:R to S,&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp; and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f(R) is a subring of S&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a subring of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Ch-3-3-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Ideals and Congruence in Rings</h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare ideal&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare ideal</span></span></span></span></span> to be a constant.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (ideal)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p>1.<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;I is a subring of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is a subring of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and</p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if r in R, i in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;r odot i in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom atom-is-selected" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;i odot r in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (ideal)&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R,oplus,odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;I is a subring of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is a subring of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let i in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let r in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;r odot i in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;i odot r in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude</em> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;I is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (principle ideal)</strong> &nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;{ z : exists r in R.z=r odot a} is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (ideal generated by two elements)</strong> &nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, a, b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;{ z : exists r in R.exists s in R.z=(r odot a) oplus (s odot b) } is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (ideal generated by three elements)</strong> &nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, a, b, c in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;{ z : exists r in R.exists s in R.exists t in R.z=(r odot a) oplus (s odot b) oplus (r odot a) oplus (t odot c) } is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__cmr">∃</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.69841em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">t</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Ch-6-1-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><h1>Arithmetic in <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;R/I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">/</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare Ker&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare Ker</span></span></span></span></span> to be a constant.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Congruent mod <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>,&nbsp; then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;cong_(I) is a relation on R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a relation on </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Congruent mod <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, a, b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a cong_(I) b&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;equiv&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;≡&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a oplus (-b) in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__cmr">−</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;cong_(I) is an equivalence relation&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> is an equivalence relation</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;R_I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;class(a) in R_(I)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;R_{I}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, A in R_(I)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;A=class(a) for some a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">A</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;R_{I}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </strong>&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, a in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;class(a) in R_(I)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, a in R, x in class(a)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x=a oplus i for some i in I&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__text"> for some </span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, a,b,c,d in R, a cong_(I) b, c cong_(I) d&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a oplus c cong_(I) b oplus d&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">and</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;a odot c cong_(I) b odot d&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.47em;"><span class="ML__center" style="top: -2.55em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span><span class="ML__center" style="top: -3em;"><span style="height: 0.43em; display: inline-block;"><span class="ML__cmr">≡</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Corollary &nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, a,b,c,d in R, class(a) = class(b), class(c) = class(d)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;class(a oplus c)=class(b oplus d)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">and</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;class(a odot c)=class(b odot d)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.66666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (definition of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\boxplus&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\boxtimes&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">⊠</span></span></span></span></span>)&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;oplus_(I):R_(I) cross R_(I) to R_(I)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;odot_(I): R_(I) cross R_(I) to R_(I)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> such that <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;if a,b in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">if </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;class(a) oplus_(I) class(b)=class(a oplus b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">and</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;class(a) odot_(I) class(b)=class(a odot b)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.69444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.77777em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (ring properties of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\Z_{}n&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__bb">Z</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span></span>) &nbsp;</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R_(I),oplus_(I),odot_(I)] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; Furthermore,&nbsp;</p>
<p>1. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If R is commutative then R_(I) is commutative&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative then </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> is commutative</span></span></span></span></span>, and&nbsp;</p>
<p>2. <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If R has identity then R_(I) has identity, 1_(R_(I))=class(1_(R))&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text"> has identity then </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__text"> has identity</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.58em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.35em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.49em; display: inline-block; font-size: 71.43%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.79444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__cmr">1</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (Kernel)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Ker(f) is an ideal of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Ker</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span> and</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x in Ker(f) equiv f(x)=0_(S)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__text">Ker</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (kernels are subrings) &nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Ker(f) is a subring of R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Ker</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a subring of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (injective Kernel)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is injective equiv Ker(f)={0_(R)}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is injective</span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__text">Ker</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.79444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (quotient map)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,\\oplus,\\odot] is a ring, I is an ideal of R, f:R to R_(I), forall x in R.f(x)=class(x)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span><span class="ML__text"> is an ideal of </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">I</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∀</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">.</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.43056em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">[</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">]</span></span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is a homomorphism&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f is surjective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is surjective</span></span></span></span></span>.&nbsp; In this case <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;f&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span></span></span></span></span> is called the&nbsp;<em>quotient map.</em></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (First Isomorphism Theorem)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R,oplus,odot] is a ring, [S,boxplus,boxdot] is a ring,f:R to S, f is a homomorphism, f is surjective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊞</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is a homomorphism</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is surjective</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;S isom R_(Ker(f))&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__cmr">≅</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.35em;"><span style="top: -2.81em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.7em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__text">Ker</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8888799999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<hr>
<p>&nbsp;</p></div>
