            <div id="document"><h1>Definition and Examples of Groups</h1>
<p>See the <a title="Modern Algebra Notes" href="https://monks.scranton.edu/files/courses/Math448/math-448-lecture.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">course notes for Modern Algebra</a> for details.</p>
<h3>Constants</h3>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Declare group, ee, abelian, card, Sym&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Declare group, </span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__text">, abelian, card</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span></span></span></span></span> to be constants.</p>
<h3>Definitions and Theorems</h3>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Group 0. </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [G,star] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;star:G cross G to G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆:</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;ee_(G) in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Group I.&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [G,star] is a group, x in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> &nbsp;<br>(identity) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;ee_(G) star x = x = x star ee_(G)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>(inverse) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x^- in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star (x^-) = ee_(G) = (x^-) star x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.821331em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size1">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size1">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.821331em;"><span class="ML__open ML__delim-size1">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.83em;"><span style="top: -3.41em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.47em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__cmr">−</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="ML__close ML__delim-size1">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Group II.&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [G,star] is a group, x, y in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;<br>(closure) <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star y in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition of Group III.&nbsp; </strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [G,star] is a group, x, y, z in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> then<br>(associativity) &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star (y star z) = (x star y) star z &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.6597200000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.6597200000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>&nbsp;Definition of Group.</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p>1. (closure)<em> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;star:G cross G to G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆:</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;i in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let x,y, z in R&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>2. (identity)&nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;i star x = x = x star i&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>3. (inverse) &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star X = i = X star x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.08em;">X</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span><br>4. (associativity) &nbsp; <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star (y star z) = (x star y) star z &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.6597200000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.6597200000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.05em;">z</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;Then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[G,star] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;i=ee_(G)&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">i</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (abelian group)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [G, star] is a group, x,y in G, G is abelian&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group, </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__text"> is abelian</span></span></span></span></span> then&nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star y = y star x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (abelian group)</strong> &nbsp;</p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R,star] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let x,y in G&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;x star y=y star x&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">x</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">y</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">x</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;G is abelian&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__text"> is abelian</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (additive group)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[R,oplus] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (group of units)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [R, oplus, odot] is a ring&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[Units(R),odot] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__cal" style="margin-right: 0.1em;">U</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: 0em; height: 0.68333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.01em;">R</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (group of units of a field)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [F, oplus, odot] is a ring, F is a field&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">F</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊕,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a ring</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">F</span><span class="ML__text"> is a field</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[F setminus {0_(F)},odot] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.25em; height: 1em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">F</span><span class="ML__cmr">∖</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.79444em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">{</span><span class="ML__cmr">0</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.33em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.48em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.14em;">F</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">}</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⊙</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (direct product)</strong></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;premise&quot;" data-shell_title="Premise:">
<p><em>Given</em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[G,star] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[H,oast] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊛</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<p><em><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;boxdot:(G cross H) cross (G cross H) to G cross H&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">⊡</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.76666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.08333em; height: 0.76666em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">(</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">)</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span></span></span></span></span></em></p>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;subproof&quot;" data-shell_title="">
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;Let r,s,u,v be such that r,u in G, s,v in H &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">Let </span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">v</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> be such that </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">v</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[r,s] boxtimes [u,v] = [r star u, s oast v]&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.625em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__ams">⊠</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.625em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">v</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.7764200000000001em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.03em;">r</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">u</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">s</span><span class="ML__ams">⊛</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.04em;">v</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Conclude &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[G cross H,boxtimes] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">×</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__ams">⊠</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span> called the direct product of <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;G &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;H&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.09em;">H</span></span></span></span></span></em>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Definition (set of permutations)</strong> &nbsp;<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If n in NN&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__bb">N</span></span></span></span></span> then</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;f in Sym_(n) equiv f:II_(n) to II_(n), f is bijective&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">∈</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__cmr">≡&nbsp;</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">:</span><span class="ML__bb">I</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">→</span><span class="ML__bb">I</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__text"> is bijective</span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;rule&quot;" data-shell_title="Rule:">
<p><strong>Theorem (symmetric group)&nbsp;</strong><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;[Sym_(n),comp] is a group&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">∘</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group</span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;card(Sym_(n))=n!&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.15em; height: 0.83333em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">∣</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.06em;">S</span><span class="ML__msubsup"><span class="ML__vlist-t ML__vlist-t2"><span class="ML__vlist-r"><span class="ML__vlist" style="height: 0.16em;"><span style="top: -2.85em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span style="height: 0.31em; display: inline-block; font-size: 70%;"><span class="ML__mathit">n</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__vlist-s">​</span></span></span></span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">∣</span></span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">n</span><span class="ML__cmr">!</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div></div>
        </div></div><div class="lurch-atom-body"><table><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><tbody><tr><td colspan="2"><b>Imported dependency document</b></td></tr><tr><td>Description:</td><td><tt>none</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Filename:</td><td><tt>learn/algebra/rules/Ch-7-1-Rules.lurch</tt></td></tr><tr><td>Source:</td><td>the web</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-refresh:</td><td>yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
            <div id="document"><p><span style="color: rgb(126, 140, 141);">Name:</span></p>
<h1 style="text-align: center;">Assignment 19</h1>
<h4 style="text-align: center;">Due: Tuesday, Nov 17</h4>
<p><span style="font-size: 11pt;">Here it is, fellow mathematicians!&nbsp; More math!</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 11pt;">Explain your answers and show work for calculations.&nbsp; Validate Lurch theorems with Lurch.&nbsp; Prove any non-Lurch theorems with a typed proof (not handwritten and pasted). You can only use theorems we covered, not theorems from future chapters.</span></p>
<hr>
<p><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><span style="background-color: rgb(45, 194, 107); color: rgb(236, 240, 241);">&nbsp; Problem 1.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>&nbsp; </span>(<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span>)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="490" height="156"></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><strong>Answer.</strong></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\square&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">□</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<hr>
<p><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><span style="background-color: rgb(45, 194, 107); color: rgb(236, 240, 241);">&nbsp; Problem 2.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>&nbsp; (</span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span><span style="font-size: 11pt;">) </span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="555" height="155">&nbsp;</span></p>
<div>Either way, prove your answer.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><strong>Proof.</strong></span></div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\square&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">□</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<hr>
<div><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><span style="background-color: rgb(45, 194, 107); color: rgb(236, 240, 241);">&nbsp; Problem 3.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>&nbsp; </span>(<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span>)</div>
<div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;theorem&quot;" data-shell_title="Theorem:">
<p><strong>Theorem (cancellation)</strong> <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;If [G,star] is a group, a,b,c in G, a star b = a star c &quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__text">If </span><span class="ML__left-right" style="margin-top: -0.19444em; height: 0.8777699999999999em;"><span class="ML__small-delim ML__open">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__small-delim ML__close">⟩</span></span><span class="ML__text"> is a group, </span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__text">, </span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">&isin;</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="ML__text"> and </span></span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span> then <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expression&quot;" data-metadata_lurch-notation="&quot;b=c&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div class="lurch-atom unindented" data-metadata_type="&quot;proof&quot;" data-shell_title="Proof:">
<p><strong>Proof.</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\square&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">□</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div><hr></div>
<div><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><span style="background-color: rgb(45, 194, 107); color: rgb(236, 240, 241);">&nbsp; Problem 4.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>&nbsp; </span>(<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span>)</div>
<div>
<div>
<div>
<div>
<p><strong>Corollary.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong><em>Every element of a finite group appears exactly once in any row or column of its multiplication table.</em>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<p><strong>Proof.</strong></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\square&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__ams">□</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<hr></div>
<div>
<div><span style="font-size: 11pt;"><span style="background-color: rgb(45, 194, 107); color: rgb(236, 240, 241);">&nbsp; Problem 5.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>&nbsp; </span>(<span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span><span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\star&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⋆</span></span></span></span></span>) A partial operation table for a group <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;\\langle G,\\star\\rangle&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__cmr">⟨</span><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__cmr">⋆⟩</span></span></span></span></span> where <span class="lurch-atom" contenteditable="false" data-metadata_type="&quot;expositorymath&quot;" data-metadata_latex="&quot;G=\\{ e, a, b, c, d, f\\}&quot;"><span class="lurch-atom-body"><span class="ML__latex"><span class="ML__base"><span class="ML__mathit">G</span><span class="ML__cmr">=</span><span class="ML__cmr">{</span><span class="ML__mathit">e</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">a</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">b</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">c</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit">d</span><span class="ML__cmr">,</span><span class="ML__mathit" style="margin-right: 0.11em;">f</span><span class="ML__cmr">}</span></span></span></span></span> is given below.&nbsp; Fill in the rest of the table.&nbsp; There is only one way to do it so that it is a group operation (it has to be associative, have an identity, and have inverses). <span style="font-size: 10pt;"><em>Hint: Use the previous two problems</em></span>.</div>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<div style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</div>
